1. Pandoc WASM core  —  GPL-2.0-or-later
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

File in this repository
    versions/v19/projects/sdcorejs-angular/services/docx/src/lib/pandoc-core.ts
    (and the mirrored copies under versions/v20 and versions/v21)

Published as
    @sdcorejs/angular/services/docx

Upstream project
    pandoc-wasm — https://github.com/pandoc/pandoc-wasm

Upstream licence
    GPL-2.0-or-later

What was taken
    The environment-agnostic pandoc core from `pandoc-wasm/src/core.js`, adapted
    to TypeScript. The file's own header states this:

        Pandoc WASM core logic — adapted from pandoc-wasm/src/core.js
        This file is a local copy of the environment-agnostic pandoc core.
        Source: https://github.com/pandoc/pandoc-wasm (GPL-2.0-or-later)

Why it was copied rather than depended on
    The `pandoc-wasm` package entry points use top-level `await`, which is not
    compatible with the esbuild/Vite pipeline Angular uses. The copy imports
    `@bjorn3/browser_wasi_shim` directly and avoids those entry points.

Scope
    This code is reached only through the `@sdcorejs/angular/services/docx`
    entry point (`SdDocxService`). No other entry point imports it. An
    application that does not import `services/docx` does not bundle it.

Related runtime artefact (not vendored)
    `SdDocxService` fetches the pandoc WebAssembly binary at runtime from
    https://pandoc.github.io/pandoc-wasm/pandoc.wasm. That binary is not
    committed to this repository and is not part of the published npm package;
    pandoc itself is GPL-2.0-or-later.

Status
    The maintainer has decided to keep this code as-is and document it here,
    rather than relicense the package or remove the entry point.


